{"id": "unknown-2026-10-14-008", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Modi Energy launches zero-upfront solar-plus-storage offer in Denmark", "content": "<p>Emaldo-backed Modi Energy says it will install, own, and operate rooftop solar and home batteries at no upfront cost to Danish households, funding a guaranteed 20% bill reduction through energy optimization and participation in power and flexibility markets. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/modi-energy-launches-zero-upfront-solar-plus-storage-offer-in-denmark/\">Modi Energy launches zero-upfront solar-plus-storage offer in Denmark</a> appeared first on <a href=\"", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/modi-energy-launches-zero-upfront-solar-plus-storage-offer-in-denmark/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-14-009", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Magenta CdTe solar panels support broccoli cultivation in agrivoltaic trial", "content": "<p>Researchers in Sweden and Italy have investigated the performance of semitransparent, magenta-colored cadmium telluride (CdTe) thin-film solar panels designed to transmit wavelengths favorable for broccoli growth. The study found that the panels affected microclimatic conditions, photosynthetic performance, nutrient composition, and overall land productivity.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/magenta-cdte-solar-panels-support-broccoli-cultivation-in-agrivoltaic-t", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/magenta-cdte-solar-panels-support-broccoli-cultivation-in-agrivoltaic-trial/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-14-010", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Panasonic unveils R454C air-to-water heat pumps for residential use", "content": "<p>The new series comprises four models with heating capacities of 3 kW, 5 kW, 7 kW and 9 kW. The units feature a refrigerant-split configuration, with the indoor and outdoor units connected by refrigerant piping.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/panasonic-unveils-r454c-air-to-water-heat-pumps-for-residential-use/\">Panasonic unveils R454C air-to-water heat pumps for residential use</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.<", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/panasonic-unveils-r454c-air-to-water-heat-pumps-for-residential-use/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-14-011", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Unico launches 330 kW bidirectional inverter", "content": "<p>The Unico GTI supports solar generation, energy storage or emerging high-power loads in a compact, rack-mounted unit, made in the USA. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/unico-launches-330-kw-bidirectional-inverter/\">Unico launches 330 kW bidirectional inverter</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/unico-launches-330-kw-bidirectional-inverter/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-14-012", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Study reveals up to 15% gap between expected and actual bifacial gains in utility-scale PV", "content": "<p>Researchers in Spain have found that the effective bifaciality of solar modules in utility-scale PV plants can be up to 15% lower than their nominal rating. Based on two years of operational data from a 50 MWp solar plant in Spain, with findings validated across four additional installations in Spain and the United Kingdom, the study highlights the influence of irradiance, temperature, mounting geometry and operating conditions on rear-side power generation.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://w", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/study-reveals-up-to-15-gap-between-expected-and-actual-bifacial-gains-in-utility-scale-pv/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-14-013", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Mercedes-Benz launches bidirectional charging in Germany", "content": "<p>Mercedes-Benz has launched a bidirectional charging service in Germany, allowing EV owners to earn payments by supplying power to the grid. The offering initially targets households without rooftop PV systems, with plans to expand to more vehicle models and markets.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/mercedes-benz-launches-bidirectional-charging-in-germany/\">Mercedes-Benz launches bidirectional charging in Germany</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-maga", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/mercedes-benz-launches-bidirectional-charging-in-germany/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-14-014", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Oswal Pumps to set up 1.2 GW TOPCon solar cell factory in India", "content": "<p>Oswal Pumps plans to invest $48 million in a TOPCon solar cell manufacturing facility in Karnal, in the Indian state of Haryana. Commercial production is expected to begin by April 2028, with the entire output earmarked for captive solar module manufacturing.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/oswal-pumps-to-set-up-1-2-gw-topcon-solar-cell-manufacturing-facility/\">Oswal Pumps to set up 1.2 GW TOPCon solar cell factory in India</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https:", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/oswal-pumps-to-set-up-1-2-gw-topcon-solar-cell-manufacturing-facility/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-14-015", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Heliup offers lightweight rooftop PV modules with waterproofing membrane", "content": "<p>French lightweight solar panel manufacturer Heliup has partnered with Holcim's Elevate brand to launch Solar Light TPO, a rooftop PV system that combines lightweight solar modules with a waterproofing membrane. The solution is designed for roofs with limited load-bearing capacity.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/heliup-offers-lightweight-rooftop-pv-modules-with-waterproofing-membrane/\">Heliup offers lightweight rooftop PV modules with waterproofing membrane</a>", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/heliup-offers-lightweight-rooftop-pv-modules-with-waterproofing-membrane/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "trina-2026-10-14-016", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["trina"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["improve", "loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Trina Solar researchers propose new classification of ultraviolet-induced degradation in TOPCon solar cells", "content": "<p>Trina Solar researchers have proposed a new classification distinguishing reversible and irreversible ultraviolet-induced degradation in TOPCon solar cells. The framework aims to improve reliability testing, identify persistent performance losses, and provide more accurate assessments of long-term module performance under real-world conditions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/trina-solar-researchers-propose-new-classification-of-ultraviolet-induced-degradation-", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/trina-solar-researchers-propose-new-classification-of-ultraviolet-induced-degradation-in-topcon-solar-cells/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-14-017", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Early backsheet removal cuts dust from thermal PV recycling", "content": "<p>Italian researchers say removing PV module backsheets before thermal recycling keeps titanium dioxide out of recovered materials and cuts particulate emissions by over one-third, but raises propane use by about 20%.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/early-backsheet-removal-cuts-dust-from-thermal-pv-recycling/\">Early backsheet removal cuts dust from thermal PV recycling</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/early-backsheet-removal-cuts-dust-from-thermal-pv-recycling/", "type": "rss"}]}
